    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n15 Leicester Avenue is a deceptively spacious 5-bedroom semi-detached family home set on a peaceful and highly sought-after residential road just off Rathgar Road. Dating from the 1930s, this attractive home extends to a generous 188 sq.m. / 2,024 sq.ft. approx. of bright, well-proportioned accommodation that is tastefully presented throughout. Offering an excellent balance of living and bedroom space, it is ideally suited to modern family living.\nArranged over two floors, the accommodation is both spacious and versatile. A bright welcoming entrance hall sets the tone for the home, leading to a bay windowed sitting room, a living room, a versatile home office / den and guest wc. To the rear, a large open-plan kitchen/ dining room forms the heart of the home, complemented by a practical utility room and enjoying direct access to the rear garden.\nUpstairs, there are five bedrooms, two of which benefit from en-suite shower rooms. A well-appointed family bathroom completes the accommodation.\nOccupying a prominent corner site, the property further benefits from good front and rear gardens, providing excellent outdoor space for both relaxation and family enjoyment.\nLeicester Avenue enjoys close proximity to the vibrant villages of Rathgar, Rathmines, Terenure and Harold's Cross, all within easy walking distance, while regular buses on the Rathgar Road makes access to the city centre very easy.\nThe area is renowned for its outstanding selection of schools, with many of Dublin's most highly regarded primary and secondary schools nearby, including Rathgar Junior School, Kildare Place School, Zion Parish School, Stratford College, Alexandra College, Gonzaga College, St Mary's College, Terenure College, St Louis and The High School.\nResidents are also spoiled for choice when it comes to leisure and recreational amenities. Nearby facilities include Brookfield Tennis Club, Rathgar Tennis Club, Milltown Golf Club and David Lloyd Riverview. The beautiful green spaces of Bushy Park, Palmerston Park, Harold's Cross Park and the Dodder Linear Park offer excellent opportunities for walking and outdoor pursuits. The surrounding villages provide an enviable array of cafés, restaurants, boutiques and artisan food shops, while the Swan Centre in Rathmines, Dundrum Town Centre and St Stephen's Green Shopping Centre are all easily accessible.\nCombining generous accommodation, mature gardens and an unrivalled location in one of Dublin 6's most convenient neighbourhoods, 15 Leicester Avenue represents a wonderful opportunity to acquire an exceptional family home."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 3.84m x 4.49m\nhall door with glazed panels, light filled hall with polished timber floor, coving, and understairs storage\n\nSitting Room - 4.47m x 4.04m\npolished timber floor continues, bay window overlooking front garden, fireplace fitted with gas fire, coving, folding doors to:\n\nLiving Room - 4.13m x 3.55m\ntimber floor continues, alcove with electric fire, coving, door to rear garden, storage cupboard\n\nKitchen / Dining - 9.35m x 4.90m\nlarge range of solid wood floor and wall units with marble effect countertop and tiled splashback, incorporating Indesit double oven, Bosch dishwasher, gas hob, sink unit with drainer, bin store, larder units and American fridge freezer, and island / breakfast bar with storage, tiled floor. Dining area with polished timber floor. Whole room is flooded with light from several windows, Velux skylight, and double door to rear garden\n\nUtility Room - 1.53m x 1.94m\nrange of floor and wall units, Beko washing machine, Hotpoint dryer, sink with drainer, tiled floor, window\n\nHome Office / Den - 2.96m x 3.10m\ntimber floor, 2 windows, coving\n\nGuest WC - \nWC, wash hand basin, tiled floor, window with opaque glass, recessed lights\n\nLanding - \nlarge landing, picture window, attic access will pull downstairs, shelved lined cupboard\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.75m x 3.59m\ndouble to front with bay window, fitted wardrobe, door to:\n\nShower en-suite - 0.86m x 2.38m\nfully tiled, step-in shower cubicle, WC, pedestal wash hand basin, extractor fan, bathroom cabinet\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.13m x 3.59m\ndouble to rear, fitted wardrobe, door to:\n\nShower en-suite - 0.86m x 2.38m\nfully tiled, step-in shower cubicle, WC, pedestal wash hand basin, extractor fan, bathroom cabinet\n\nFamily bathroom - 2.45m x 2.60m\nfully tiled, bath with hand shower attachment, WC, pedestal wash hand basin, bathroom cabinet, corner shower cubicle with Mira Elite SE electric shower\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.95m x 2.60m\nBright single to rear with dual aspect 2 windows, free standing wardrobe\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.20m x 2.60m\nbright single to front, fitted wardrobe\n\nBedroom 5 - 3.20m x 2.65m\nbright single to front with fitted wardrobe\n\nOutside - \nPedestrian access to front garden which is walled, railed and lawned with mature trees and shrubs, on street permit parking, Pedestrian side access to the rear garden which is private and measures 6.5m x 12m approx. A patio area is positioned off the living room, and garden is lawned and bordered by tall walls. There is a part enclosed side passageway, very useful for bins, bikes storage etc, outside tap.\n\n"
